{
	"_about": "The village festivals (Festivals, scripts/festivals/festivals.gd; README.md, Festivals). One per season, all our own: names, dates, hours and looks were made up for Harvest Son. Per festival: name (HUD tag and calendar), season, day, hours [\"H:MM\", \"H:MM\") on the map where it is held, place (the cell it gathers round, [x, y]; `--festival=<id>` starts the farmer there facing up), event (data/events, plays once a year when the farmer is on the map in the hours), closes (shop ids from data/shops.json that stay shut all day), props (decorations on the map during the hours: {kind, cell, size?}; not solid, so they never block a walk; looks in FestivalProps / FestivalView), optional fireworks [\"H:MM\", \"H:MM\") (bursts over the 3D view in those hours). DESIGN: a festival day is always sunny (the weather rolled for it is replaced the evening before). Optional contest: {name, takes (the kind of entry: crop, fish, animal for eggs / milk / wool, mine for the mine's ores and stones), table (a cell of a judge_table prop; E there with an entry overhead enters it, empty-handed the judge says the `ask` line of data/dialogue/contests.json), in_season (score factor for an entry that grows in the festival's season), rivals [{who (a villager), score [lowest, highest]}] rolled once per festival and year, prizes by place [{money, item?, count?}], event (data/events, the results; flags contest_place_<n> and contest_won_<rival> are set for its lines)}. An entry scores its shipping value; one entry a year; the farmer wins ties. Optional stall: {id?, name, cell (a cell of a stall prop), stock [{item, price?}]}, or a list of them (each with its own id), a shop (id stall:<festival>, or stall:<festival>:<stall id>) that sells only in the festival's hours; its stock is set out on the stall's counter in both views, and the other stall props are only looks. Placing in a contest also gives a ribbon (data/keepsakes.json). Prize money is kept small: a first prize is about a good day's shipping.",
